
# Cockpit runtime state (sidecar port/url) — regenerated per launch
.cockpit/

# Project inbox — external material staged for triage (LIFECYCLE.md).
# Gitignored because an item is either filed (and the FILED artefact is what
# gets committed) or discarded. Committing staging would preserve exactly the
# thing triage exists to resolve.
# Anchored: an unanchored `inbox/` matches a directory of that name at ANY
# depth, so a `docs/features/inbox/` would vanish from the repository with
# no error anywhere (project-os-cockpit ISS-0070 — a whole feature and three
# tasks were missing from a fresh clone, which then failed the validator).
/inbox/
